WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.640
What makes code click?

2
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:07.280
Here, you learn one idea at a time and put
it to work straight away: first

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:12.220
you read a short explanation with a worked
example, then you fill the gaps

4
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.900
in code that's already started, then you
fix a mistake and watch what changes,

5
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.220
and finally you write the code yourself,
using everything you've practised.

6
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:26.440
The task stays beside your editor while
you work, so you can run your code

7
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:31.340
to see its output, submit your answer for
instant feedback on what to check next,

8
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.680
and use that feedback to revise and try
again, opening one hint at a time whenever

9
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.740
you need a nudge.

10
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.200
Step-through diagrams let you follow the
code as the table changes, and you can go

11
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.880
back to compare any step with the one
before it.

12
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.940
It all runs in your browser with nothing
to install;

13
00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:55.120
the free R courses are open now, and SQL
and Python are coming in December,

14
00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.260
so start your first lesson today.
